# Sample Form\* component with best practices

Follow this example when creating a new form component.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import * as z from "zod";

// ALWAYS define a zod schema for the form
// ALWAYS place it at the top of the file
const schema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1),
  email: z.string().email("Invalid email"),
});

type Schema = z.output<typeof schema>;
// ALWAYS export the schema type
export type FormUserData = Schema;

// ALWAYS include the following props in the component:
type Props = {
  defaultValue?: Partial<Schema>;
  loading?: boolean;
};

// Use withDefaults when it makes sense to do so
const props = withDefaults(defineProps<Props>(), {
  defaultValue: () => ({}),
  loading: () => false,
});

// Initialize the state with the defaultValue props
const state = reactive<Partial<Schema>>(props.defaultValue);
// ALWAYS watch for changes in the defaultValue props
watch(
  () => props.defaultValue,
  (v) => v && Object.assign(state, v),
);

// ALWAYS deinfe a 'submit' event of the type Schema
const emits = defineEmits<{ submit: [e: Schema] }>();
</script>

<template>
  <!-- ALWAYS set the .prevent modifier to the submit event -->
  <UForm
    :schema="schema"
    :state="state"
    :loading="loading"
    class="flex flex-col gap-4"
    @submit.prevent="(e) => emits('submit', e.data)"
  >
    <UFormField name="name" label="Name" description="Enter your name">
      <UInput
        v-model="state.name"
        placeholder="Ex: John Doe"
        class="w-full"
      />
    </UFormField>

    <UFormField name="email" label="Email" description="Enter your email">
      <UInput
        v-model="state.email"
        type="email"
        placeholder="Ex: john.doe@example.com"
        class="w-full"
      />
    </UFormField>

    <div class="flex gap-2 justify-between items-center mt-4">
      <UButton type="submit" label="Submit">
    </div>
  </UForm>
</template>
```

## Key Guidelines

- Always use TypeScript with `z.output<typeof schema>` for type safety
- Use `reactive<Partial<Schema>>({})` for form state
- Use `withDefaults` for props with default values
- Export form data type: `export type FormData = Schema`
- Initialize state from props: `name: props.defaultValue?.name ?? ''`
- Use `watch` to sync props changes to state: `watch(() => props.defaultValue, v
=> v && Object.assign(state, v))`
- Use `@submit.prevent` with direct emit: `@submit.prevent="(e) =>
emits('submit', e.data)"`
- Use `class="flex flex-col gap-4"` for form layout
- Use `description` prop on `UFormField` for help text
- Use slots for submit button customization: `<slot name="submit-button">`
- Use `defineEmits<{ submit: [e: Schema] }>()` for simple emit patterns
- Handle form submission with `FormSubmitEvent<Schema>` when using handler
  functions
- Access form methods via template refs: `const form = useTemplateRef('form')`
- Common validation: `validate-on` prop controls when validation triggers
- Error handling: Listen to `@error` event for custom error handling
